rthermore, it details various nitrogen solutions used for parenteral nutrition, providing information on their composition and nutritional values, which is essential for healthcare providers in administering appropriate nutritional support.\n\nMoreover, TABLA 1 provides mandatory nutritional information per 100 g/100 ml, ensuring that users have access to standardized data for dietary planning. Lastly, it outlines the Mini Nutritional Assessment-Short Form (MNA-SF) criteria, which are used to evaluate nutritional status, thereby aiding in the identification of individuals at risk of malnutrition. Overall, TABLA 1 serves as a vital tool in the fields of nutrition and dietetics, offering a multifaceted approach to dietary management and assessment.", "ALIMENTACIÓN ORAL:Alimentación oral refers to the process of consuming food by mouth. This method may be transitioned to after enteral nutrition in stable patients. It is particularly significant in the management of patients with intestinal failure, as it plays a crucial role in their nutritional care. However, the ability to engage in alimentación oral can be affected in patients experiencing malnutrition or gastrointestinal issues. Therefore, the safety of oral feeding is often evaluated in patients who have been receiving enteral nutrition to ensure that they can safely consume food through the mouth.", "TRASTORNOS DE LA CONDUCTA ALIMENTARIA:\"TRASTORNOS DE LA CONDUCTA ALIMENTARIA\" refers to a range of psychological conditions that significantly impact eating behaviors and the relationship individuals have with food. These disorders, which include anorexia nerviosa (AN) among others, are characterized by abnormal or disturbed eating habits. They can complicate the management of obesity and necessitate specialized treatment approaches. Additionally, eating disorders can develop in children who are subjected to prolonged enteral nutrition, further affecting their relationship with food. Overall, \"TRASTORNOS DE LA CONDUCTA ALIMENTARIA\" encompasses various psychological disorders that require careful attention and intervention.", "FÓRMULAS HIPOCALÓRICAS:Las fórmulas hipocalóricas son preparaciones alimenticias que no tienen indicaciones pediátricas específicas.", "FÓRMULAS NORMOCALÓRICAS:Las fórmulas normocalóricas son indicadas en la mayoría de los pacientes pediátricos, proporcionando un aporte calórico adecuado.", "FÓRMULAS HIPERCALÓRICAS:FÓRMULAS HIPERCALÓRICAS son preparaciones nutricionales específicamente diseñadas para ofrecer un alto contenido calórico. Estas fórmulas son especialmente útiles para pacientes que presentan descompensación hidrópica y son utilizadas en situaciones donde hay un aumento de las necesidades calóricas, como en el caso de pacientes con desnutrición. Su objetivo principal es proporcionar la energía necesaria para apoyar la recuperación y el bienestar de estos pacientes.", "SONDAS GÁSTRICAS Y YEYUNALES:Las sondas gástricas y yeyunales son dispositivos utilizados para la administración de nutrición enteral, adaptándose a las necesidades del paciente.", "ÍLEO GÁSTRICO:El íleo gástrico es una condición médica caracterizada por el retraso en el vaciamiento del estómago, frecuentemente observado en el periodo postoperatorio inmediato. Esta condición implica una obstrucción en el proceso de vaciamiento gástrico, lo que puede llevar a la necesidad de nutrición enteral para asegurar la adecuada ingesta de nutrientes.", "FÍSTULAS PANCREÁTICAS:Las fístulas pancreáticas son conexiones anormales que pueden formarse entre el páncreas y otros órganos, a menudo requiriendo nutrición enteral para evitar la estimulación de la secreción pancreática.", "VACIAMIENTO GÁSTRICO:", "PICA PERCUTÁNEA:Pica percutánea is a medical procedure used for gastrostomy in patients, except those with severe thoracic and spinal deformities, malrotation, previous abdominal surgery, obstructions, and esophageal stenosis.", "SONDAS DE GASTROSTOMÍA:Gastrostomy tubes are medical devices used for feeding patients who cannot eat by mouth, which can be replaced after three months once the gastrocutaneous fistula is formed.", "SISTEMAS DE INFUSIÓN:Infusion systems are methods used to deliver nutrients to patients, including gravity drip and pump systems, with specific applications in pediatric and critical care.", "FÓRMULAS:Formulas refer to nutritional solutions designed for infants and children, tailored to their specific dietary needs based on age and health conditions.", "RN A TÉRMINO:RN a término refers to nutritional formulas for full-term newborns when breastfeeding is not possible."], "parameters": {"model": "text-embedding-3-small", "temperature": 0.0, "frequency_penalty": null, "presence_penalty": null, "top_p": 1.0, "max_tokens": 4000, "n": 1}, "history": null}